The setup and init dispatch tests no longer touch the repo root; they write into a tempdir instead. The full cargo test, clippy -D warnings and fmt --check passed, and .yoyo.toml was unmodified before every commit. The one part I didn't finish is the census of other tests that might write to the repo (see the end).

What changed
• **src/dispatch_sub.rs:** `try_dispatch_subcommand(args)` is now a one-line wrapper around `try_dispatch_subcommand_in(args, project: Option<ProjectIo>)`. `ProjectIo { dir, input } is only read by the setup and init` branches.
  • With None (normal use), those branches make the same calls as before: run_setup_wizard() and handle_init().
  • With `Some, setup goes through the existing dir-taking wizard (run_wizard_interactive_in(dir, input, stdout)) and init goes through a new handle_init_in(dir)`.
• **`src/commands_project.rs:** handle_init() now calls handle_init_in(current_dir().unwrap_or_default())`. The paths and printed messages are the same as before.
• Tests: both moved to src/dispatch_sub_project_tests.rs (declared #[cfg(test)] in main.rs, the same way commands_risk_epistemic_tests is). This kept dispatch_sub.rs from absorbing them.
  • They still go through the full dispatcher, so each one fails if setup or init stops routing.
  • The setup test feeds scripted answers (4\n\n1\n: ollama, default model, save to project), so it never asks for a key or reads the environment. It checks that .yoyo.toml appears in the tempdir and that the repo's .yoyo.toml bytes are the same before and after.
  • The init test checks that YOYO.md appears in the tempdir and does not appear in the repo root.
  • No env vars are set in either test.
• **`tests/module_size.rs:** updated the size limits for two grandfathered files: dispatch_sub.rs 2162 → 2166 and commands_project.rs` 3640 → 3645. Both are within the 100-line drift band.
• **`ARCHITECTURE.md:** new src/dispatch_sub.rs` entry covering the incident, the fix and the census.

Not verified
• **The census is incomplete.** I listed all 39 `test_try_dispatch_subcommand_*` tests but didn't trace their handlers, so it isn't a proven "0 other writers". I wrote down five candidates as unchecked: _commit, _update, _todo/_todo_list/_memories (possible .yoyo/ writes), and _risk_bare (possible append to the snapshot ledger). Tracing those handlers is the follow-up.
• **No positive control.** I didn't run the old test in a throwaway worktree to watch it clobber `.yoyo.toml`, because I ran out of context budget. The evidence that the fix routes to the tempdir is that the new assertions find the file there.

I committed three wip: #962 checkpoints plus the final commit 97b1f743.
